{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For one moment I would go up in your midst and consume you.</b> If I go up in your midst and you are rebelling against Me with the stubbornness of your neck, I would be wrathful against you for one moment — that is the measure of His wrath, as it says: ״חֲבִי כִמְעַט רֶגַע עַד יַעֲבָר זָעַם״ (Isaiah 26) — and consume you. Therefore it is better for you that I send an angel." "<b>And now.</b> This punishment shall befall you immediately — that you take off your ornaments from upon you." "<b>And I will know what to do to you.</b> At the reckoning of the rest of the sin, I know what is in My heart to do to you."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:18.586269101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}